D. Embedding theorem toy readout
  predicate=contains color chain 0 -> 1 -> 2 as a rooted homeomorphic path
  coarse quotients leak under one-step outer extension.
  small_embedding_profile is already pure in the bounded n<=6, 3-color toy.
  address_plus_small_embedding is the LRC-shaped channel: extension address plus embedding downset.

E. Greedy finite bad sequence miniature
  control=size<=step through 5
  greedy_length=5
  sequence:
    1: size=1 height=1 0
    2: size=2 height=2 1(1)
    3: size=3 height=2 1(2,2)
    4: size=4 height=2 2(1,1,1)
    5: size=5 height=2 2(1,1,2,2)
  reading=finite bad sequences are easy to build locally; the hard theorem is the uniform no-infinite-bad-sequence/controlled-miniature bound.

F. Tournament Analysis
  vertices=quotient/address channels
  observable=(exactness,max_bucket,compression,embedding_naturality,LRC_transfer,action)
  score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1, 6: 1}
  directed_3cycles=0
  scc_sizes=[1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]
  hamiltonian_paths=1
  top_order:
    address_plus_small_embedding
    small_embedding_profile
    full_embedding_profile
    outer_address
    frontier
    color_hist
    size_height

G. Repo transfer
  Outer extension usability theorem (repo form): a quotient is usable only if every allowed outer extension has a retained address that keeps the target predicate pure.
  Outer extension embedding theorem (repo form): the natural address is the bounded embedding/downset profile plus the extension address.
  LRC14 translation: Res_27 is the internal tree, +27 carry is outer extension, owner-private deletion is the first small embedding address.
